sub:assertion {
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/problem/somite-number-control> a delphi:Concept, schema:Question ;
    rdfs:label "What sets vertebrate somite number?" ;
    dct:description "Across vertebrates, is total somite (and hence vertebral) number set by the ratio of the duration of axis elongation to the segmentation-clock period, as clock-and-wavefront predicts, and if so what evolutionary changes in clock period and elongation explain the range from about 30 to over 300?" ;

    skos:historyNote "Known state: Cooke and Zeeman (1976) proposed clock-and-wavefront; Gomez et al. (2008) showed in zebrafish, chick, mouse and corn snake that snakes make many more somites by slowing axis elongation relative to the clock; Oates, Morelli and Soroldoni (2012) review the clock. Clock period and elongation rate are measured in only a handful of species, so the comparative prediction has not been tested broadly. Already a Frontier Problem." ;
    dct:subject "biology" ;
    delphi:hypothesisType "open-problem/tier-B" ;
    skos:scopeNote "Resolved when: A pre-registered comparative test: for every species with a measured clock period and elongation duration, compare predicted and observed vertebral counts (from museum and literature counts via the organisms layer); state in advance the tolerance for 'supports'." ;
    skos:scopeNote "Resolved when: A ranked list of species whose clock measurement would most reduce uncertainty about the mechanism." ;
    skos:scopeNote "Refuted if: Measured clock period and elongation duration whose ratio mispredicts somite number by more than the stated tolerance in several species." ;
    skos:note "Data access: Vertebral counts in literature and museum databases (open); clock periods from published time-lapse studies." ;
    skos:note "Requires: developmental-biology" ;
    skos:note "Requires: comparative-data" ;
    skos:note "Requires: data-test" ;
    skos:note "Scale: developmental" ;
    skos:note "Scale: evolutionary" ;
    skos:note "Also recorded as a Delphi Frontier Problem: Somite number control" ;
    skos:related <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/thompson1917-ch17-04> ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://doi.org/10.1016/S0022-5193(76)80131-2> ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://doi.org/10.1038/nature07020> ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://doi.org/10.1242/dev.063735> ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://github.com/fractastical/delphi/blob/e77f4bcffb077981b60f1e3aea24b72c7a36b2fc/problems/problems.json> .

  <https://doi.org/10.1016/S0022-5193(76)80131-2> dct:title "A clock and wavefront model for control of the number of repeated structures during animal morphogenesis" ;
    dct:bibliographicCitation "Cooke and Zeeman 1976, A clock and wavefront model for control of the number of repeated structures during animal morphogenesis" .
  <https://doi.org/10.1038/nature07020> dct:title "Control of segment number in vertebrate embryos" ;
    dct:bibliographicCitation "Gomez et al. 2008, Control of segment number in vertebrate embryos" .
  <https://doi.org/10.1242/dev.063735> dct:title "Patterning embryos with oscillations: structure, function and dynamics of the vertebrate segmentation clock" ;
    dct:bibliographicCitation "Oates, Morelli and Soroldoni 2012, Patterning embryos with oscillations" .
}

